# <%= current_page.data.title %>

Troubleshooting in Ingestion can take several forms. This page includes some steps that can help, each situation is different however and can require investigation beyond what is outlined below.

> **It is recommended that you always confirm with any user that reports an issue with Ingestion the following details:**
>
> - name of file sent
> - time file is sent
> - the environment if this is not clear - you can usually establish this from the ticket and looking at the users in the configuration
>
> This will:
>
> - aid troubleshooting
> - ensure that a file has been uploaded
>
> **AVOID troubleshooting without a confirmation either from the user or that it is immediately apparent in the logs that a file has been uploaded.**

## Finding Lambda logs

Each Lambda function has logs in CloudWatch. The primary functions to look at when troubleshooting are, in order, are `transfer`, `scan` and `definition-upload`.

To access logs, open the function, select the **Monitor** tab, then choose **View CloudWatch Logs**.

> **Note**
>
> CloudWatch Logs group multiple transfers/scans etc into one log stream. One log stream ≠ one event / file upload / file scan. Multiple transfers / scans can be included in one CloudWatch log.

## Understanding transfer logs

Transfer logs outline activity in a simple timestamped manner. Note the filename and destination is included.

```shell
2025-10-14T14:14:48.096Z
START RequestId: a15be7b6-8ce0-4bc9-a541-19c9235e6478 Version: $LATEST

2025-10-14T14:14:48.097Z
Supplier: analytical-platform

2025-10-14T14:14:48.097Z
Object: file.txt

2025-10-14T14:14:48.440Z
Successfully copied analytical-platform/file.txt to mojap-land-dev/analytical-platform/file.txt

2025-10-14T14:14:48.640Z
Successfully deleted analytical-platform/file.txt from mojap-ingestion-development-processed

2025-10-14T14:14:48.640Z
handler.py completed successfully!

2025-10-14T14:14:48.642Z
END RequestId: a15be7b6-8ce0-4bc9-a541-19c9235e6478

2025-10-14T14:14:48.643Z
REPORT RequestId: a15be7b6-8ce0-4bc9-a541-19c9235e6478 Duration: 546.56 ms Billed Duration: 2915 ms
```

If you cannot see expected logs for a file in question check the `scan` lambda logs. The scan is triggered when the file first lands in the S3 bucket.

